{
  "literal_corrections": 14,
  "corrections": [
    {
      "source_file": "host/common-errors-diagnostics.mdx",
      "id": "MCL-8ba507584c40e9c8",
      "start": 166,
      "end": 166,
      "before": "Correlate timestamps with self-test runs, rentals, `gpu-burn`, or other load tests. Repeated messages during load are much more concerning than a small number of corrected messages during boot.",
      "after": "Correlate timestamps with self-test runs, rentals, `gpu-burn`, or other load tests. Record the frequency and whether AER labels the events corrected, uncorrected non-fatal, or fatal. Corrected errors are recovered by hardware; recurring events merit investigation, and uncorrected events require particular attention.",
      "after_spans": [
        {
          "source_file": "host/common-errors-diagnostics.mdx",
          "start": 166,
          "end": 166,
          "text_sha256": "362a97d43d4a2249f6e41145a74b23a703fd512bc87f3dccee9ad9775359140f"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "source_file": "host/disable-ssh-password-login.mdx",
      "id": "CUR-722204a43ad1f31d",
      "start": 139,
      "end": 141,
      "before": "`sshd -t` checks the config for errors. The `&&` means the restart only runs if\nthat check passes, so a broken config cannot take SSH down. Editing the config\nchanges nothing until you restart.",
      "after": "`sshd -t` checks configuration validity and key sanity. The `&&` runs the\nrestart only after that check succeeds; it cannot guarantee a successful\nrestart or continued access. Configuration edits affect the daemon after it\nreloads or restarts.",
      "after_spans": [
        {
          "source_file": "host/disable-ssh-password-login.mdx",
          "start": 139,
          "end": 142,
          "text_sha256": "2cec7af23449c8db9ca3556a34dff0f1894daabc3fe527d94c0785ff8eb2a14d"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "source_file": "host/disable-ssh-password-login.mdx",
      "id": "CUR-4f4370d23549cda8",
      "start": 166,
      "end": 167,
      "before": "If it still says `yes`, most likely no config file had the setting. Add it,\nthen restart and check again:",
      "after": "If it still says `yes`, inspect which global setting or applicable `Match`\nblock supplies that value, including files read by `Include`. Set the relevant\n`PasswordAuthentication` directive to `no`, then validate, apply and check again:",
      "after_spans": [
        {
          "source_file": "host/disable-ssh-password-login.mdx",
          "start": 167,
          "end": 169,
          "text_sha256": "8dcae1126df5a6f95896b6b818153cf7291824a4e63f9f776fec3f170ca294e2"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "source_file": "host/disable-ssh-password-login.mdx",
      "id": "CUR-8a9ed935fa6b7c35",
      "start": 178,
      "end": 179,
      "before": "Once the output is `passwordauthentication no`, you are done. If your machine\nwas flagged for password login, the error clears within about two hours.",
      "after": "After applying the changes, confirm that a separate key-only SSH connection\nworks before closing the original session. Recheck the machine’s status; if\nthe password-login warning persists, contact support with the current warning\nand the relevant configuration checks.",
      "after_spans": [
        {
          "source_file": "host/disable-ssh-password-login.mdx",
          "start": 180,
          "end": 183,
          "text_sha256": "6daa5ce6fa0c2e362717b2d8a5820d0d9fd06ece8bf651d8dd7f7555efb0842e"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "source_file": "host/machine-errors.mdx",
      "id": "MCL-3b35a3450b691d5d",
      "start": 37,
      "end": 37,
      "before": "| Logged only | The message is recorded against a specific rental attempt and does not de-verify or unlist the machine by itself. | Container create, build, volume, template-update, or secrets-service messages | Use the message as support context if the rental failed or repeats. |",
      "after": "| Logged only | The message is recorded against a specific rental attempt and does not de-verify or unlist the machine by itself. | The container, build, volume, template-update, and secrets-service messages listed under [Rental-Attempt Messages](#rental-attempt-messages); machine authentication denied (HTTP 401) is a VM-offer error. | Use the exact message as support context if the rental failed or repeats. |",
      "after_spans": [
        {
          "source_file": "host/machine-errors.mdx",
          "start": 37,
          "end": 37,
          "text_sha256": "c982b00664cad1118805bd5724bcc8a59b6616fb444c609c9137bcbcfcc32046"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "source_file": "host/machine-errors.mdx",
      "id": "MCL-ea8a2aa0b8266bc6",
      "start": 85,
      "end": 85,
      "before": "A UDP failure can still happen when the UDP port appears mapped and the container-side responder starts. The public UDP path still has to work end to end. The paid dogfood run on 2026-06-24 reproduced this shape: the TCP progress endpoint was reachable, but the external UDP echo probe timed out. Treat this as a network-path issue first, not a CUDA or NCCL failure.",
      "after": "A UDP port mapping and a running container-side responder do not establish that the public UDP path works end to end. If TCP succeeds but an external UDP echo probe times out, investigate UDP forwarding and the return path first. TCP success alone does not establish UDP reachability.",
      "after_spans": [
        {
          "source_file": "host/machine-errors.mdx",
          "start": 85,
          "end": 85,
          "text_sha256": "cfc409e70bc96ce3d68dea1a4ab456797d22aa640f583b08e208f927a20cf3c5"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "source_file": "host/machine-errors.mdx",
      "id": "MCL-f9df4750dc665783",
      "start": 169,
      "end": 169,
      "before": "Corrected AER at boot can be harmless, but repeated messages during load are a stronger signal. See [Host Diagnostics: GPU PCIE Issue](/host/common-errors-diagnostics#gpu-pcie-issue).",
      "after": "Corrected AER events are recovered by hardware. Record their timing and frequency, distinguish them from uncorrected or fatal events, and investigate recurring errors. See [Host Diagnostics: GPU PCIE Issue](/host/common-errors-diagnostics#gpu-pcie-issue).",
      "after_spans": [
        {
          "source_file": "host/machine-errors.mdx",
          "start": 169,
          "end": 169,
          "text_sha256": "aa0d88288a6989ef0c57fcc43ad817301be32bf0dc0ab83a2fc55906e6553a6d"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "source_file": "host/machine-errors.mdx",
      "id": "MCL-6b3a48733434c5e5",
      "start": 174,
      "end": 174,
      "before": "`bad bandwidthtest2` means a GPU transfer or bandwidth health check failed. Treat it as a machine-health or verification error.",
      "after": "`bad bandwidthtest2` with `not r_H2D or not r_D2H or not r_D2D` reports a failed GPU transfer sanity check. The [Crypto Labs operator wiki](https://www.cryptolabs.co.za/vast-ai-gpu-hosting-wiki/?wiki_page=common-errors) describes possible causes, including a GPU falling off the bus and driver/runtime problems. Check GPU visibility and daemon/kernel logs before resetting the machine.",
      "after_spans": [
        {
          "source_file": "host/machine-errors.mdx",
          "start": 174,
          "end": 174,
          "text_sha256": "571ed9b0bf8e57669a301e4891facca546426dd6c22a310ef4bb7a3d97643d82"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "source_file": "host/machine-errors.mdx",
      "id": "MCL-790a4747eda0a70a",
      "start": 191,
      "end": 191,
      "before": "If a GPU has fallen off the bus, power-cycle the host and fix the hardware path before listing again.",
      "after": "If a GPU has fallen off the bus, collect the Xid and kernel logs and follow your hardware vendor’s recovery guidance. Coordinate any reset or power cycle with active rentals; confirm GPU and container health before listing again.",
      "after_spans": [
        {
          "source_file": "host/machine-errors.mdx",
          "start": 191,
          "end": 191,
          "text_sha256": "6756a29461325ee87cc1a9d0dcf79c42ebc41596d2a201e5070209f743f0d6aa"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "source_file": "host/machine-errors.mdx",
      "id": "MCL-fbdc4691cbb74f9d",
      "start": 206,
      "end": 206,
      "before": "If the error repeats, remove the machine from active hosting until the GPU is repaired or replaced.",
      "after": "If the error repeats, stop accepting new work and follow NVIDIA or your hardware vendor’s ECC diagnosis and recovery guidance. Coordinate recovery with active rentals; the required action may include a reset, row remapping, repair, or replacement, depending on the GPU and exact error.",
      "after_spans": [
        {
          "source_file": "host/machine-errors.mdx",
          "start": 206,
          "end": 206,
          "text_sha256": "24730e92b8e63fe5e79b73d85f539d5181f13dc2fce994eed2eadb90701e3577"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "source_file": "host/machine-errors.mdx",
      "id": "MCL-2c0a05172822d57e",
      "start": 218,
      "end": 218,
      "before": "`nccl_failed` or NCCL initialization/synchronization errors mean multi-GPU communication failed after the test started.",
      "after": "`nccl_failed` or NCCL initialization/synchronization errors mean the NCCL test could not initialize or complete its communication checks. Read the detailed error: a setup or initialization failure does not show that GPU-to-GPU communication ran.",
      "after_spans": [
        {
          "source_file": "host/machine-errors.mdx",
          "start": 218,
          "end": 218,
          "text_sha256": "35b9c645c0e8a0294e5a5c2a747465d586410f83744c631bc424138f641fcf89"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "source_file": "host/machine-errors.mdx",
      "id": "MCL-d5fcb8a06ce549a2",
      "start": 238,
      "end": 238,
      "before": "Vast uses Docker storage quotas for renter containers. Do not bypass the error by removing Docker quota settings. Move or remount `/var/lib/docker` onto the intended XFS filesystem, enable `pquota` or `prjquota` in `/etc/fstab`, verify quota state, then restart Docker and host software.",
      "after": "Vast uses Docker storage quotas for renter containers. Do not bypass the error by removing Docker quota settings. Plan storage changes around active rentals and preserve renter data. Configure the intended XFS filesystem for `/var/lib/docker` with `pquota` or `prjquota` in `/etc/fstab`; quota accounting must be enabled when the filesystem is mounted. Verify the backing mount and quota state before restarting Docker and host software.",
      "after_spans": [
        {
          "source_file": "host/machine-errors.mdx",
          "start": 238,
          "end": 238,
          "text_sha256": "5bc93833832a0862eccc71dcafb3671778d6a0c77246d1a2c6ef688dbb681c24"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "source_file": "host/machine-errors.mdx",
      "id": "MCL-75f7b6edfb04fc5b",
      "start": 255,
      "end": 255,
      "before": "Do not manually delete renter data. For expired or deleted rentals that did not release storage, use [vastai cleanup machine](/cli/reference/cleanup-machine).",
      "after": "Do not manually delete renter data. For expired storage instances, review and use [vastai cleanup machine](/cli/reference/cleanup-machine). If deleted rentals still appear to occupy storage, collect Docker usage and mount details for Vast support.",
      "after_spans": [
        {
          "source_file": "host/machine-errors.mdx",
          "start": 255,
          "end": 255,
          "text_sha256": "5b2833e30f84a634ab61143ac62bb76b98966b938e3f9566d7cbfde14b0b3bf2"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "source_file": "host/machine-errors.mdx",
      "id": "MCL-1221941af8a7a4fe",
      "start": 52,
      "end": 52,
      "before": "| `bad bandwidthtest2` | GPU transfer or PCIe bandwidth health | [`bad bandwidthtest2`](#bad-bandwidthtest2) |",
      "after": "| `bad bandwidthtest2` | GPU transfer sanity check | [`bad bandwidthtest2`](#bad-bandwidthtest2) |",
      "after_spans": [
